# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build. The API image
# needs only the root pyproject.toml and uv.lock, api/, and
# eval/pyproject.toml (see Dockerfile). Everything else stays local -- above
# all .env, which must never reach a build or an image (ADR 0004).
#!include:.gitignore

# Re-include the crime datasets that .gitignore excludes.
#
# .gitignore still carries "api/app/crime/*.csv" and "*.geojson" from before
# these files were moved to Git LFS. They are tracked, so git ignores those
# rules entirely -- git never applies an ignore rule to a file already in the
# index, which is why `git check-ignore` reports them as not ignored.
#
# gcloud has no such concept. It reads the included patterns as plain globs
# and strips both files from the upload, so `COPY api/app api/app` copies a
# directory without them and every /crime request fails at the spatial join
# with "No such file or directory". That is why address lookup has never
# worked in a deployed environment -- it works locally, where the files are
# simply on disk.
#
# Negations must come after the include or they have no effect.
!api/app/crime/*.csv
!api/app/crime/*.geojson

.git
.github/
web/
docs/
supabase/
scripts/
api/tests/
api/scripts/
eval/*
!eval/pyproject.toml

**/__pycache__/
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.env
.env.*
Claude outputs/

